---
import ReferenceLayout from '@layouts/ReferenceLayout.astro';
import { getReference } from '@data/reference';

const ref = getReference('target-heart-rate-table')!;
---

<ReferenceLayout reference={ref}>
  <Fragment slot="intro">
    Your maximum heart rate and the main training zones by age, in beats per minute — a quick reference for
    keeping exercise at the right intensity.
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="howto">
    <h2>How to use this chart</h2>
    <p>
      Find your age and read across. <strong>Max HR</strong> is the estimated ceiling (220 − age).
      <strong>Fat burn</strong> (60–70%) is easy, sustainable effort; <strong>aerobic</strong> (70–80%) builds
      cardio fitness; <strong>anaerobic</strong> (80–90%) is hard interval work. Most training mixes the zones.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="notes">
    <h2>Methodology</h2>
    <p>
      Maximum heart rate uses the common 220 − age estimate, and each zone is a percentage of that maximum,
      computed with this site's unit-tested target-heart-rate function. Individual maximums vary by 10–20 bpm.
      For personalised zones using your resting heart rate (the more accurate Karvonen method), use the
      <a href={`/${ref.relatedCalculator}`}>target heart rate calculator</a>. Consult a doctor before starting
      intense exercise. This is general information, not medical advice.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</ReferenceLayout>
